From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 02:38:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Reuse scratch block positions in the World query loops

Each of these loops allocated a MutableBlockPosition per call, and they
run several times per entity per tick; a live-server profile attributed
~14 MB/min of BlockPosition allocation to them.

They now take a per-thread scratch position instead. Every call site owns
a fixed slot, so a nested query cannot scribble over the position another
one is still iterating with, and none of these methods is reentrant with
respect to itself. The position was already reused across each loop, so
sharing it between calls adds no new aliasing that the old code did not
already have.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

